    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter bc16be3cd91b1d7508f91da97f5c95881eea5fc7 custom operator is dot-repeated in full even if it itself executes dot-repeatable action in the process.\n\nI personally think that this is an improvement and how it should work. Although *technically* this is a regression that diverges from Vim behavior and might cause problems with some plugins. So decided to report this for posterity, but would be in favor of closing this as \"as expected\".\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create the following `init.lua`:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- A composite action with dot-repeatable action as a part of it\n    _G.operator = function()\n      vim.fn.setreg('\"', '_xxx')\n      -- Nested dot-repeatable action\n      vim.cmd('normal! $p')\n    end\n    \n    local rhs = function()\n      vim.o.operatorfunc = 'v:lua.operator'\n      return 'g@'\n    end\n    vim.keymap.set('n', 'gh', rhs, { expr = true })\n    \n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, { 'aaa' }\n    ```\n\n2. `nvim --clean -u init.lua`\n3. While the cursor is at line start, type `ghl`. It adds `xxx` at the end of the line.\n4. Press `^` to navigate to the start of the line and press `.`. It again adds `_xxx` at the end of the line (i.e. repeating the whole operator). When before bc16be3cd91b1d7508f91da97f5c95881eea5fc7 it would add `_xxx` at cursor (i.e. repeating the last dot-repeatable action from `normal! $p`).\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe current behavior is what I'd initially expect from dot-repeating a custom operator. However, this might be considered a regression, so decided to open an issue for posterity.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1471+gca992e82d4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nProbably, no (didn't verify)\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.1.11-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage and from source",
